{"title":"The Surly Steamroller Is Back, Wearing “Frank or Beans” for Blue Lug’s 20th","link":"https://bikerumor.com/the-surly-steamroller-is-back-wearing-frank-or-beans-for-blue-lugs-20th/","date":1795097779000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-hero.jpeg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" alt=\"(Photos / Surly Bikes)\" /></p>\n<p>A few days ago, Surly went ahead and dug the Steamroller out of retirement. They brought it to a friend and long-time Surly dealer, Blue Lug, the famous Japanese bike shop. The Surly x Blue Lug Steamroller collaboration is to celebrate the iconic shop’s 20th anniversary.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"1033\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637.jpeg\" alt=\"Surly X Blue Lug Limited Steamroller first pic\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637-297x240.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637-120x97.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637-768x620.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-first-pic-e1794943616637-1115x900.jpeg 1115w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photos / Surly Bikes)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Look, if you don’t follow along much, Blue Lug has been in the news a bit <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/velo-orange-teams-with-japans-iconic-blue-lug-for-new-escargot-cargo-bike/\" target=\"_blank\">lately</a>. They’re a shop known for excessively drool-worthy bike builds and tasty <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/camp-and-go-slow-collaborates-with-japans-blue-lug-bike-shop-for-alt-cycling-at-its-best/\" target=\"_blank\">collaborations</a>. I mean, beautiful. The special-edition Steamroller frameset comes in a colorway called Frank or Beans, and it’s pretty awesome. It’s a glossy, copper-tinged brown with rose-gold Surly lettering and a Surly x Blue Lug decal on the down tube. Fancy, but not fussy. Ya know?</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-seat-cluster-e1794943587884.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"843\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-seat-cluster-e1794943587884.jpeg\" alt=\"Surly X Blue Lug Limited Steamroller seat cluster\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-seat-cluster-e1794943587884.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-seat-cluster-e1794943587884-297x196.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-seat-cluster-e1794943587884-120x79.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-seat-cluster-e1794943587884-768x506.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you missed the first go-round, the Steamroller debuted in 2000, rode the fixie boom, became a messenger staple, and ran for 23 years. Now it’s back for a limited time as a frameset only. Complete bike? Nope. That’s your job.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"1026\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104.jpeg\" alt=\"Surly X Blue Lug Limited Steamroller frameset\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104-297x238.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104-120x96.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104-768x616.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-frameset-e1794943549104-1123x900.jpeg 1123w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The recipe hasn’t changed much, which is the point. The main triangle is double-butted 4130 chromoly, TIG-welded, paired with a brazed 1-1/8″ threadless chromoly fork. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"855\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605.jpeg\" alt=\"Surly X Blue Lug Limited Steamroller rear dropout\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605-768x513.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-rear-dropout-e1794943510605-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Steamroller Geometry</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Geometry leans road, but the details lean track: 120mm rear spacing, a track-legal 275mm BB height, and track crank compatibility. The one update is new cable guides for cleaner rear brake routing.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1.png\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1629\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1.png\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1.png 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1-297x242.png 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1-1536x1251.png 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1-120x98.png 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1-768x626.png 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/surly-geo-drawing-gravel-2000x1505-1-1105x900.png 1105w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><table><tbody><tr><th>Size</th><th>49cm</th><th>53cm</th><th>56cm</th><th>59cm</th><th>62cm</th></tr><tr><th>A. Effective Top Tube</th><td>528.0</td><td>546.0</td><td>568.0</td><td>588.0</td><td>609.0</td></tr><tr><th>B. Stand Over</th><td>754.0</td><td>784.0</td><td>812.0</td><td>839.0</td><td>869.0</td></tr><tr><th>C. Reach</th><td>388.0</td><td>394.0</td><td>403.0</td><td>408.0</td><td>420.0</td></tr><tr><th>D. Stack</th><td>505.0</td><td>531.0</td><td>559.0</td><td>586.0</td><td>618.0</td></tr><tr><th>E. Total Seat Tube Length</th><td>515.0</td><td>555.0</td><td>585.0</td><td>615.0</td><td>645.0</td></tr><tr><th>F. Headtube Length</th><td>83.0</td><td>109.0</td><td>136.0</td><td>163.0</td><td>196.0</td></tr><tr><th>G. Headtube Angle</th><td>72.5</td><td>73.0</td><td>73.5</td><td>74.0</td><td>74.0</td></tr><tr><th>H. Seat Tube Angle</th><td>74.5</td><td>74.0</td><td>73.5</td><td>73.0</td><td>73.0</td></tr><tr><th>I. BB Drop</th><td>70.0</td><td>70.0</td><td>70.0</td><td>70.0</td><td>70.0</td></tr><tr><th>J. BB Height</th><td>275.0</td><td>275.0</td><td>275.0</td><td>275.0</td><td>275.0</td></tr><tr><th>K. Chainstay Length</th><td>398.0</td><td>398.0</td><td>398.0</td><td>398.0</td><td>398.0</td></tr><tr><th>L. Fork Length Axle to Crown</th><td>375.0</td><td>375.0</td><td>375.0</td><td>375.0</td><td>375.0</td></tr><tr><th>M. Fork Offset</th><td>38.0</td><td>38.0</td><td>38.0</td><td>38.0</td><td>38.0</td></tr><tr><th>N. Wheelbase</th><td>957.0</td><td>967.0</td><td>979.0</td><td>988.0</td><td>1008.0</td></tr><tr><th>Crank Arm Length</th><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><th>Handlebar Width</th></tr><tr><th>Recommended Rider Height</th><td>160.0 – 170.0</td><td>168.0 – 178.0</td><td>173.0 – 188.0</td><td>185.0 – 196.0</td><td>193.0 – 203.0</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Brakes are rim-only, with the fork and seatstay bridge drilled for mid-reach (47-57mm) calipers. Tire clearance tops out at 38mm without fenders, or 32mm with them, and only the rear gets fender eyelets.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-bb-e1794943644386.jpeg\"><img width=\"1280\" height=\"860\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-bb-e1794943644386.jpeg\" alt=\"Surly X Blue Lug Limited Steamroller bb\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-bb-e1794943644386.jpeg 1280w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-bb-e1794943644386-297x200.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-bb-e1794943644386-120x81.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-bb-e1794943644386-768x516.jpeg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>There’s one bottle mount. No derailleur hanger, no rack mounts, no apologies. The frame is powder-coated over an E-coat for rust resistance, and a 56cm weighs 6 lb 14 oz. Which, BTW, is pretty respectable for steel that’s meant to get ridden hard and locked up outside in the elements.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers.jpeg\"><img width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers.jpeg\" alt=\"Surly X Blue Lug Limited Steamroller stickers last\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Surly-X-Blue-Lug-Limited-Steamroller-stickers-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>Surly X Blue Lug Steamroller Retail &amp; Detail</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Retail: $699 (frame and fork)</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Road bike geometry with track bike features: 120mm rear spacing, track-legal BB height, track crank compatible</li>\n\n\n\n<li>100% Surly 4130 chromoly steel frame and fork; double-butted main triangle, TIG-welded</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Brake cable stops for cleaner rear brake routing</li>\n\n\n\n<li>1-1/8″ threadless chromoly steel fork, brazed</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fork and seatstay bridge drilled for mid-reach (47-57mm) caliper brakes</li>\n\n\n\n<li>700c x 38mm maximum tire clearance without fenders (32mm with fenders — rear fender eyelets only)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>One bottle cage mount</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Frame is powder-coated for a durable finish and E.D. coated for rust resistance</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Sizes run 49 to 62cm. When we checked Surly’s site, every size showed as “sold out online” except 59cm, so if you want one, start pestering your local shop. Details at the link below.</p>\n\n\n\n<p> <em><a href=\"https://surlybikes.com/\" target=\"_blank\">SurlyBikes.com</a></em></p>","author":"Ron Frazelle","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/the-surly-steamroller-is-back-wearing-frank-or-beans-for-blue-lugs-20th/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"f7596dad8008e6d4b324305485347b15c96d9b3f41692ea4312d4c10ff719016","category":"Cycling"}